WEBVTT

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:07.010
I ate too much shaved ice and 
gave myself a stomachache.

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:10.360
What? Sh-Shaved ice?

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:15.360
I've only just been able 
to escape the bathroom.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.690
Enjoy the game.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.320
What's his deal?

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.880
And he's giant. He must be
at <i>least</i> as big as Iwashimizu.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.630
No, he's bigger than Iwashi.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.130
He's the 192-centimeter,

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.630
98-kilo ace of Ryoin Academy.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:40.140
Their #8...

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:45.850
Zanba Ryujin.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:30.350
Kazama!

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:33.250
How many times have you been late this month?!

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.620
Sorry, Coach.

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:38.820
<b>Episode 11
You Have No Feel For the Game</b>

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:40.540
The strawberry shaved ice was 
just so good, I ate too much of it.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:43.890
You're unbelievable!

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:48.110
You'll have to make up 
for this after the game.

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:49.390
Coach.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:55.900
I ran here from home. I'm already warmed-up.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:00.610
Ref, we're making a substitution.

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:05.950
The #9, Zanba Ryujin, is coming on.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.390
Huh? That's not the #8 shirt.

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:11.120
What position does #9 play?

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.060
Scrum-half. That's my position.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:14.590
What?

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.690
Wait, this doesn't make any sense!

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:19.160
The scrum-half is the bridge

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:24.070
that links the play from the big 
forwards to the ball-carrying backs.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:28.620
That position requires 
quick passing and agility,

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:31.060
so a lot of scrum-halfs are small.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:35.890
What the hell is a 192 cm tall guy
doing playing scrum-half?

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:38.700
You're late, Ryujin.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.720
Sorry.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.380
Zanba.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:44.250
It's Zanba.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.100
What will he do?

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:53.960
Ryujin!

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:56.480
What kind of pass will he throw?

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.760
Stop Zanba!

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:08.890
Kota.

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.520
Got it.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:14.500
Wh-What's going on? His passes seem slow.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:16.020
And when he's holding the ball...

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:20.900
...he just charges forward.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:23.360
I see.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.890
What does it mean?

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:28.660
You know you're only allowed to pass 
the ball backwards in rugby, right?

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:29.670
Yeah.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:34.420
So the guy holding the ball is 
always leading his team forward.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:39.540
Imagine a line extending from him.
The team can only pass behind it.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.720
They can't play the ball
in front of that line.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:46.930
The more they pass, the less space
 they have to continue the play.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:51.250
If your passes are slow, your opponents 
will gobble up more and more of the field.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:54.080
That's why most teams 
pass the ball around quickly

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:55.940
and run forward with it 
to control more of the field.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:05:00.890
But in his case, he only needs to 
charge forward and throw one pass,

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:04.680
as he's claimed so much 
of the field on his own.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:06.200
That's how it works.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.060
Knock-on by Ryoin!

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:14.220
Wow. I'm really sorry.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:15.830
What are you doing, Ryujin?!

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.240
Yeah!

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:18.750
It's finally our ball!

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.090
We're just getting started! Let's punish them!

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.010
Crouch.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.760
Bind. Set!

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:33.850
Zanba's not the only one.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:37.060
All of Ryoin's forwards 
are strong and skillful.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.860
Crap! They'll move the ball out to the wing!

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:42.860
What? They're not?

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:45.110
Straight down the middle?

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.370
He's not passing?!

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:15.180
Try!

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:24.600
Normal scrum-halfs move the ball sideways.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:30.950
But Zanba uses his muscle and power 
to take the ball down field.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:34.200
He's not really a scrum-half...

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:40.670
He's the ninth forward on the team.

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:48.220
The ninth forward?

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.720
Think of it as having two Sekkis on a team.

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:53.000
"Sekki"?

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:53.850
Sekizan.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:54.990
Oh, snap!

00:06:55.810 --> 00:07:00.460
They're unreal. The champions 
of Kanagawa are a cut above.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:05.050
We shouldn't have come to watch them.

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:07.730
Huh? Did you say something?

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:10.990
Oh... uh...

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:14.770
Nothing.

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:23.000
Ryoin crushed them 91-0. 
That was incredible.

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:25.470
That was so much fun!

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:29.510
It actually kinda depressed me.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:34.630
This place sells rugby stuff.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.430
New cleats, huh?

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:43.770
Come to think of it,
you've been using my old ones.

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:46.570
Yeah. What should I get?

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:51.700
As long as you're not a fatso, 
you can play just fine in soccer cleats.

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:55.890
But if you've got the money, 
you can get some pretty nice ones.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:58.450
It goes without saying that they're 
comfortable to wear, but also...

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:01.460
They can make you go,
"I'm feeling a little different today."

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:04.090
and be a mysterious source of motivation.

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:07.460
But I don't have any money.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:08.700
Of course you don't.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.700
These are so cool...

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:13.050
But they're super expensive!

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:15.640
Gion.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:20.060
What did you think after watching 
an amazing team like Ryoin play?

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:28.390
Since we're aiming for the Nationals at 
Hanazono, we'll end up facing Zanba.

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:31.320
I still can't visualize that.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.740
I know what you mean.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:34.800
But it sounds like it'd be fun.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:38.440
I'll train hard so I can knock 
that Zanba character off his feet.

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:41.450
I'll practice by tackling Iwashimizu 
since he's almost as tall.

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:47.230
What did you think of their 
pint-sized flanker?

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:51.090
He was awesome, too.
I'd love to hear his thoughts on stuff.

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:57.390
But, when it comes to awesome 
pint-sized guys, I think I prefer you.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:05.570
When I watch you,
it's like you enjoy being short.

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:06.850
I think it's inspiring.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:10.020
Being short does bother me, too, you know.

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:13.860
But I think of my height as an asset.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:19.850
I used to get mad when people 
mentioned my height, just like you.

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:20.990
Seriously?

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:24.940
My buddy Kashi—I mean, Kashima...

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:29.000
<b>Rugby Team</b>

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:27.620
He was the only one invited 
to join the rugby team

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:29.000
during our first year of middle school.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:34.300
It annoyed me, so I joined before he could.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.520
Wow.

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:38.580
If they didn't want short players,
it just made me want to join all the more.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.160
I have a terrible personality.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:43.350
Teach me, O Wise One...

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:47.130
But the going got tough once I'd joined.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:49.990
Kashi played in his first game before I did.

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:53.610
I constantly thought about quitting.

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:56.860
Now, here's your question...

00:09:56.860 --> 00:10:00.110
How did Kamo-kun get back on his feet?

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:02.160
Tick tock, tick tock, tick tock...

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:02.160
Uh...

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:04.620
Bzzt. Time's up.

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:10.380
The correct answer is "the words 
of a truly brilliant foreign winger."

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:14.050
"Small people...

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:20.840
have tons of space."

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:33.240
It means I can run into spaces 
too small for Sekki to fit through.

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:36.440
People who impart wisdom
like that are the best.

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:40.470
I drew a lot of courage from those words.

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:43.050
I stopped getting mad
when people called me short.

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:49.320
But I don't use my small stature 
as well as that flanker does.

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:52.840
I need to get better at that.

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:56.170
Technique and strategy 
are important, of course.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:11:00.260
But when you start out, the thing 
that surprisingly has the most effect...

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:04.330
on your play is the words 
of some famous player...

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:07.540
or slightly overpriced cleats.

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:12.050
AKA being a simpleminded idiot.

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:15.800
All right. I'm going to ask my mom 
if I can buy some expensive cleats.

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:19.030
Don't blame me if they don't help your game.

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:23.030
I like you, too.

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:25.950
This all reminds me of 
being in middle school.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:28.540
It's what they call
"returning to your roots," I guess.

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:32.490
After watching Ryoin's game today...

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:37.840
For a moment, I thought there was no way
we could beat them.

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:41.950
You won't know that until you try.

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:47.180
That little flanker was incredible,
so he's my goal.

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:48.770
I'm going to be a flanker.

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:53.270
Our flankers are Hyoyan and Sugayan.

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:53.270
<b>Hyosu</b>

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:53.270
<b>Kasuga</b>

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:56.410
They're both idiots, so I'm not 
sure they'll be able to teach you.

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:57.520
I see.

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.480
I can't... reach...

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:00.310
Which ones?

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:03.780
The orange ones.

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:12.570
Kokuto, if you're going to 
buy something, hurry it up.

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:14.450
I want to go to the bookstore.

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:17.270
Okay, Sekito. Just give me a minute.

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:19.680
Jeez...

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:26.760
I want to go grab my pre-ordered copy
 of <i>Miraculous Ririn-chan</i>'s Volume 12.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:29.140
It's the number one flanker!

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:35.040
<b>This mysterious Ryoin 

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:35.040
<b>related to anyone

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:38.020
<b>He appears a few times

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:38.020
<b>Did you see him? 

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:41.690
We just watched your game!

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:44.910
Teach me how to be a flanker!

00:12:45.220 --> 00:12:47.760
Where did this come from? And who are you?

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:49.910
I want to go read
the new volume of Ririn-chan.

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:52.290
"Ririn-chan"?

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:56.130
You mean that "Miraculous Ru-Ririn" show?

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:05.090
I'm so glad I've met someone 
I can talk to about Ririn-chan!

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:08.070
My brother likes it.
We watch the anime every week.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:10.870
This week's episode had godlike animation!

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:13.270
I can't believe you watch anime, Gion.

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:15.100
What's it about?

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:16.850
Well...

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:19.110
Miraculous Ru-Ririn!

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:21.880
Ririn-chan doesn't know
how to use her magic staff,

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:25.990
so she bludgeons her enemies to death,

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:28.310
and a fairy follows her around 
trying to set her straight.

00:13:28.310 --> 00:13:30.250
What kind of story is that?

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:32.640
But I prefer Rurun-chan.

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:35.620
Rurun-chan is great! You have good taste!

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:37.540
Is he always like that?

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:38.630
Yeah.

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:40.600
You should come over to my place sometime!

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:43.090
I bought the box set! 
Let's watch it together!

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:46.970
No, thanks. I wanted to ask you about rugby.

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:50.560
About rugby?

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:56.230
Yeah. Why did you decide to become a flanker?

00:13:57.810 --> 00:13:59.260
Because Ririn-chan...

00:13:59.260 --> 00:14:01.060
I like strong people.

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:03.070
...said that on her show.

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:04.890
Seriously?

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:07.680
I thought rugby would make me stronger.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:09.070
Our school's team is really good.

00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:11.590
I thought I'd rather be 
a forward than a back.

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:15.660
And considering my height,
flanker was the only position I could play.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:17.020
Seriously?

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:19.920
Yeah. He started in high school.

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:24.600
I'm a beginner, so I don't know anything.

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:27.260
What does a flanker do?

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:29.260
Everything.

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:36.600
Whether it's attacking or defending, 
they're the first ones on the scene.

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:40.660
They arrive at the goal line 
quicker than everyone else.

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:43.110
They have to participate in every play.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:46.650
The position with the most responsibilities 
on the team is the flanker.

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:49.420
It's Rurun-chan.

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:50.410
<b>Rurun-chan</b>

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:53.630
What am I going to do?

00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:56.290
There are so many things I can't do.

00:14:57.570 --> 00:14:59.660
What should I start with?

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:03.290
Why do you want to play flanker so badly?

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:07.680
At first, it was because I 
was told I'd be good at it.

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:10.010
But?

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:14.010
But now, it's because I look up to you!

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:20.390
Rurun, why did you become my friend?

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:22.890
It's simple.

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:26.900
Because I look up to you!

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:30.650
That's a classic Rurun-chan quote! Yes!

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:33.900
I like you. What's your name?

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:35.610
Gion.

00:15:35.610 --> 00:15:38.910
Gion, I'll test you right now.

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:40.910
Come on.

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:48.610
Let's play tag here.

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:49.580
What?

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:52.470
I'll see if you'd make a good flanker.

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:56.220
If you can catch me, I'll give you
this Rurun-chan sticker, too.

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:00.490
I'll do it.

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:03.690
I don't really care about 
the sticker, though.

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:06.440
No touching the ground, okay?

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:09.030
I'm over here.

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:14.780
Over here.

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:19.040
Dammit.

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:22.410
Wow, your brother's really agile.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:24.530
Well, yeah.

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:28.170
A flanker needs speed and 
a good sense of balance.

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:30.730
What might have seemed like a stupid idea...

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:33.340
could actually be a good way 
to measure if he's fit for the position.

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:49.110
I don't think you'll ever catch me.

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:52.610
We can play normal tag.

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:22.600
You have less feel for 
the game than I thought.

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:26.190
You wouldn't make a good flanker.

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:33.230
Wait.

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:35.350
One...

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:38.660
One more time!

00:17:40.250 --> 00:17:42.790
I'm next.

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:46.220
What, Kokuto? It's pointless.

00:17:46.720 --> 00:17:48.990
There's something I want to see.

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:52.840
Try getting past me. You're on offense.

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:56.590
I'll only move sideways.

00:17:57.130 --> 00:18:00.870
Try to get past me as though
 you're running with the ball.

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:03.970
Okay!

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:06.810
Come on!

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:10.010
There's no way he can do it.

00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:15.600
Most people are too scared to move when 
up against someone as huge as Kokuto.

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:17.740
What's he looking for?

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.490
You know, he and I are pretty similar.

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:33.250
We're both used to seeing
big guys all around us.

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:42.390
Dammit.

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:52.060
Are you okay, Gion?

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:56.400
Being used to something isn't enough.

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:26.030
Don't do anything crazy.

00:19:27.400 --> 00:19:28.640
See?

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:33.480
Ow...

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:38.280
Sekito.

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:40.440
He's you, Sekito.

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:41.280
What?

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:43.280
What does that mean, Kokuto?

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:46.280
I'm...

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:49.600
joining the rugby team.

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:52.040
Unlike you, I'm a beginner.

00:19:52.430 --> 00:19:56.540
But in this new volume, we learned 
what Ririn-chan's type is.

00:19:57.540 --> 00:20:00.050
She likes strong people.

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:02.090
What?

00:20:03.610 --> 00:20:05.600
You think this is cakewalk, Kirishima?!

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:10.550
You're not going home until 
you make 20 more tackles!

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:14.600
He's puking again. You're in the way!

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:16.610
Isn't he an otaku?

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:17.610
Gross.

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:21.010
What's your brother thinking?

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:24.180
Kokuto...

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:27.290
I want to practice.

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.230
Come to the park with me.

00:20:40.680 --> 00:20:42.710
That's all wrong!

00:20:42.710 --> 00:20:45.890
You couldn't even knock over 
a grade school kid with that tackle!

00:20:50.130 --> 00:20:52.190
You have no feel for the game!

00:20:53.110 --> 00:20:55.400
You should quit!

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:58.240
No! No!

00:20:58.240 --> 00:21:01.150
I'm going to get stronger!

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:05.150
One more time! One more time!

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:11.040
Sekito used to be worse than you.

00:21:11.670 --> 00:21:15.040
He couldn't make wild and forceful attacks,

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:20.800
nor could he fearlessly charge 
into larger opponents.

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:24.880
I think you'd make a good flanker.

00:21:26.210 --> 00:21:28.930
Whether or not you have
a feel for the game...

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:32.510
just determines how quickly 
or slowly you progress.

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:34.700
Good luck.

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:39.940
Your refusal to give up 
is just like Sekito's.

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:43.120
I'm sure you'll get stronger.

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:49.850
When I get stronger, please play us!

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:52.080
Our team's called Jinko.

00:21:56.630 --> 00:21:57.900
I'll remember that.

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:50.030
<b>Next Time: "Joint Practice"</b>

00:23:45.770 --> 00:23:48.120
Next time: "Joint Practice!"
